subproblem.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ and let X ∈ 𝒟_n(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ n) be integer multiplicity with spt X compact. Then there is an IMRep R in ℝ^P representing X with R.carrier ⊆ spt X and μ_R(ℝ^P) = R.measure univ < ∞. Moreover, there are, for i ∈ ℕ, Lipschitz G_i : ℝ^n → ℝ^P, Borel A_i ⊆ ℝ^n, and measurable w_i : ℝ^n → ℤ and c_i : ℝ^n → ℝ such that:
- G_i is differentiable at every point of A_i, and G_i(A_i) ⊆ spt X;
- w_i is Lebesgue integrable on A_i;
- for u ∈ A_i, c_i(u) ≥ 0 and |α(DG_i(u)e_0, …, DG_i(u)e_{n−1})| ≤ c_i(u)·|α| for every n-covector α (e_a = EuclideanSpace.single a 1, |α| = covectorEuclideanNorm α);
- Σ_i ∫⁻_{A_i} |w_i|·c_i dL^n < ∞;
- for every test form γ ∈ 𝒟^n(ℝ^P), the series Σ_i ∫_{A_i} w_i(u)·γ(G_i(u))(DG_i(u)e_0, …, DG_i(u)e_{n−1}) du converges to X(γ) (HasSum).
(Step 7 of the parent proof, with the Jacobian weights replaced by the covector bounds c_i.)

